   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Dative and accusative together",
   "texto": [
    "With verbs like **schenken** (gift), **geben** (give) and **zeigen** (teach) goes first the **dativo** (to whom) and then the **acusativo** (what): **Ich schenke meiner Mutter Blumen** (I give flowers to my mother). Question: **Wem?** (who to?) and **Was?** (what?).",
    "With pronouns, the order changes: the accusative goes before the date: **Ich gebe es ihm** (I give it to him)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "In-dative pronouns",
   "texto": [
    "You saw: **mir**, **dir**, **ihm**, **ihr**, **uns**, **euch**, **Ihnen**, **ihnen**. With **ihr** (to it) the verb can go behind: **Ich schenke ihr Blumen**.",
    "Eye with the false friend: **geben** means «give» and not «be»."
   ]
